WEBVTT

00:01.700 --> 00:04.551
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.222 --> 00:08.507
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.542 --> 00:12.077
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.095 --> 00:15.064
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:15.098 --> 00:18.584
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.602 --> 00:21.871
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.905 --> 00:23.456
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.490 --> 00:24.807
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.841 --> 00:26.841
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.418 --> 00:37.786
Oh, Stewie,
how exciting!

00:37.820 --> 00:39.938
Your first visit to
a real fire station!

00:39.972 --> 00:43.041
Yeah, you kids always loved your
first trip to the fire station.

00:43.075 --> 00:44.359
You remember when we took Meg?

00:48.214 --> 00:50.882
Welcome to the Quahog
Fire Department, folks.

00:50.917 --> 00:52.217
I'm Captain Beckman.

00:52.251 --> 00:53.385
Let me know if you
have any questions

00:53.419 --> 00:54.552
that I can
answer for you.

00:54.587 --> 00:56.054
JOE:
What's up, nerds?

00:56.088 --> 00:59.291
You waiting for some guy to
fall asleep with a cigarette?

00:59.325 --> 01:00.892
Lazy fire turds!

01:00.927 --> 01:02.560
Have another donut, pig!

01:02.595 --> 01:04.629
We got guns! You got hoses!

01:04.664 --> 01:06.331
See you on the softball field!

01:11.737 --> 01:14.723
Over here is our kitchen,
where we make all our meals.

01:14.757 --> 01:16.458
And upstairs
is where we sleep.

01:16.492 --> 01:18.259
What about your
wives and families?

01:18.294 --> 01:20.962
Sometimes we don't see them
for long periods of time.

01:20.997 --> 01:22.897
Well, that sounds
awfully lonely.

01:22.932 --> 01:25.267
Like being an NBA player
on the road.

01:25.302 --> 01:27.370
Baby, I miss my wife so much.

01:27.404 --> 01:29.205
Thanks for understanding
that we can't do anything.

01:29.239 --> 01:30.606
I just want to cuddle.

01:30.641 --> 01:32.008
Oh, you're so sweet.

01:32.042 --> 01:33.776
I'm just doing
what a man should do.

01:33.810 --> 01:36.312
Respecting the sacred
institution of marriage.

01:36.346 --> 01:38.381
And now, straight to sleep.

01:38.415 --> 01:40.983
<i>ANNOUNCER: This message brought
to you by the NBA.</i>

01:41.018 --> 01:42.652
<i>Let's all pretend this happens.</i>

01:42.686 --> 01:45.154
Hey, Chris, you think it's safe
to drink from a fire hose?

01:45.205 --> 01:46.939
Why not, Dad?
It's just water.

01:46.974 --> 01:48.958
All right, well, turn it on.
I'm very thirsty.

01:51.345 --> 01:52.561
Nice job, Chris.

01:52.596 --> 01:54.096
You got my shirt wet.

01:54.131 --> 01:55.665
Now, few people realize

01:55.699 --> 01:58.267
that until 1928
there were no hoses,

01:58.301 --> 02:01.237
and you actually had to fight
fires with your bare hands.

02:01.271 --> 02:03.272
I will now give
a demonstration.

02:08.195 --> 02:09.195
(grunts)

02:11.264 --> 02:13.416
Whoa, scrappy little blaze, huh?

02:13.450 --> 02:15.468
Oh, my God,
the fire's got a gun!

02:18.439 --> 02:20.207
What the (bleep) was that?

02:20.241 --> 02:22.242
(making driving noises)

02:23.811 --> 02:24.945
Come on, Stewie.
We're going.

02:24.979 --> 02:26.179
Just a moment, Brian.

02:26.214 --> 02:27.514
I'm pretending
I'm a fireman.

02:27.548 --> 02:29.216
I love playing pretend.

02:29.250 --> 02:31.902
My name's Peter
and I work in the brewery.

02:31.936 --> 02:33.336
Now I'm gonna put on my pants

02:33.371 --> 02:34.905
and go talk
to my coworkers at...

02:34.939 --> 02:36.473
These pants have
stool in them.

02:40.428 --> 02:43.697
Well, I hope everyone had a fun
afternoon at the firehouse.

02:43.731 --> 02:45.132
I sure did, Mom!

02:45.166 --> 02:48.318
I can't wait for the
next family outing!

02:50.354 --> 02:51.822
Aw, thanks, Mike.

02:51.856 --> 02:53.256
I hate fire stations.

02:53.291 --> 02:55.258
(man's voice): No problem, man.
(sniffing)

02:55.293 --> 02:57.360
Is that alcohol
on your breath?

02:57.395 --> 02:58.612
Yeah, maybe.

02:58.646 --> 03:01.148
You're playing this
too fast and loose, Mike!

03:05.603 --> 03:06.903
Ooh, ooh, is
that the mail?

03:06.938 --> 03:08.572
Yeah.
Is there anything in there for me?

03:08.606 --> 03:09.973
I want to see if
there's a response

03:10.007 --> 03:11.641
to all those fan letters
I've been writing.

03:11.676 --> 03:13.678
<i>PETER:
Dear Cary Elwes,</i>

03:13.712 --> 03:16.414
<i>I have been meaning to
contact you for some time.</i>

03:16.448 --> 03:19.484
<i>I have never been able to
figure out if you are famous.</i>

03:19.518 --> 03:21.385
<i>You were a big deal
in one thing,</i>

03:21.420 --> 03:24.222
<i>but you were wearing
a mask for most of it.</i>

03:24.256 --> 03:26.724
<i>Do you consider your
career a disappointment?</i>

03:26.759 --> 03:29.627
<i>Or rather, did you exceed
your own expectations?</i>

03:29.661 --> 03:31.896
<i>Yours truly, Peter Griffin.</i>

03:31.930 --> 03:35.199
<i>P.S. You were in
Robin Hood: Men in Tights.</i>

03:35.234 --> 03:37.068
<i>Did you know that?</i>

03:37.102 --> 03:39.237
Hey, there's something here
from the Nielsen Company.

03:40.272 --> 03:41.906
"Dear Griffin family,

03:41.940 --> 03:44.776
"You have been specially
selected from amongst millions

03:44.810 --> 03:47.678
"of American households
to be a Nielsen family,

03:47.713 --> 03:51.315
"and as such, to have your
TV viewing habits monitored

03:51.350 --> 03:54.252
in order to measure
television ratings."

03:54.286 --> 03:57.522
Oh, kids, this came
all the way from Delaware.

03:57.556 --> 03:58.956
What does all
that mean?

03:58.991 --> 04:01.409
Well, Meg, it sounds like
they want us to be part of

04:01.443 --> 04:03.744
a select group of people that
helps determine what's on TV.

04:03.762 --> 04:05.196
We're gonna be a Nielsen family?

04:05.230 --> 04:06.197
That's awesome!

04:06.231 --> 04:08.233
(somber, sad music plays)

04:10.069 --> 04:11.170
I think... uh...

04:11.204 --> 04:13.038
I think that's
the wrong music.

04:13.072 --> 04:15.641
(victorious fanfare plays)

04:15.675 --> 04:17.209
There you go.

04:24.105 --> 04:27.173
Now, this Nielsen box will keep
track of everything you watch,

04:27.208 --> 04:29.509
which helps us generalize
the viewing habits

04:29.543 --> 04:31.077
of millions of Americans.

04:31.112 --> 04:32.512
Ah, yes.

04:32.546 --> 04:34.581
And what was that beginning,
middle and end part again?

04:34.615 --> 04:35.949
Um...

04:35.983 --> 04:39.219
this Nielsen box will keep track
of everything you watch,

04:39.253 --> 04:41.321
which helps us generalize
the viewing habits

04:41.355 --> 04:42.822
of millions of Americans.

04:42.857 --> 04:44.941
Is there any way you can
describe that to me

04:44.975 --> 04:46.459
using colorful puppets
of some sort?

04:48.479 --> 04:51.781
The Nielsen box will monitor
your viewing habits!

04:51.816 --> 04:53.116
(scratchy laugh)

04:53.150 --> 04:56.786
I don't like the left puppet.
His chin is scary.

04:58.389 --> 05:00.256
Well, thanks
for your cooperation.

05:00.291 --> 05:02.359
If you have any questions,
please call me.

05:02.394 --> 05:04.095
And welcome
to the Nielsen family.

05:04.129 --> 05:06.697
Thank you very much.

05:06.731 --> 05:08.149
Well, isn't this exciting.

05:08.183 --> 05:10.317
I know, I can't believe
we're a Nielsen family!

05:10.352 --> 05:12.236
I never get picked
for anything.

05:16.358 --> 05:18.375
(people screaming)

05:28.787 --> 05:29.920
All right, everyone.

05:29.955 --> 05:31.489
Time to do
our Nielsen duty.

05:31.523 --> 05:32.823
So, what are we gonna watch?

05:32.858 --> 05:34.258
<i>Boobs!
Project Runway!</i>

05:34.292 --> 05:36.494
<i>The Good Wife!
That black version of our show!</i>

05:36.528 --> 05:38.529
You know, guys, this
is a real opportunity

05:38.563 --> 05:40.030
to promote quality
programming.

05:40.065 --> 05:41.415
I think we should
watch PBS.

05:41.449 --> 05:43.417
Yeah, you're real
passionate about PBS.

05:43.451 --> 05:46.554
You donated once five years ago
and they sent you a mug.

05:46.588 --> 05:49.056
And now the mug's so old
that the "P" has been worn off

05:49.090 --> 05:50.407
so it just says "B.S."

05:50.442 --> 05:53.077
It's libtards like you that are
screwing up our country.

05:53.111 --> 05:55.914
(knock at door)

05:55.948 --> 05:57.916
Tom Tucker?
What are you doing here?

05:57.950 --> 05:59.584
Well, I heard you're
the new Nielsen family.

05:59.619 --> 06:01.786
Just hoping you plan to watch
the Channel Five News.

06:01.821 --> 06:03.588
I don't know.
I've missed so many.

06:03.623 --> 06:05.223
It's gonna take me
forever to catch up.

06:05.258 --> 06:07.159
Well, we'd sure love
to have you as a viewer.

06:07.193 --> 06:08.393
Is there anything we can do

06:08.427 --> 06:09.839
to make the news
more appealing to you?

06:09.864 --> 06:10.929
Maybe.

06:10.930 --> 06:12.631
I guess you could
lose the moustache.

06:12.665 --> 06:13.832
Lose my moustache?

06:13.866 --> 06:15.834
Well, gosh, I...
I don't know.

06:15.868 --> 06:17.335
My birthmark
makes it kind of tough.

06:17.370 --> 06:19.704
Always caused me problems
at my old job.

06:19.739 --> 06:22.140
And that'll do it for us here
at Channel 12 News.

06:22.175 --> 06:23.742
Make sure you turn
those clocks ahead.

06:23.776 --> 06:25.076
Good night, St. Louis.

06:25.111 --> 06:26.278
Yeah, I don't know,

06:26.312 --> 06:28.013
I was never that crazy
about the moustache.

06:28.047 --> 06:30.248
Well, I suppose I could lose it
and just use more makeup.

06:30.283 --> 06:31.650
Yeah, that'd be cool.

06:31.684 --> 06:33.985
And maybe a festive hat would
make things more festive.

06:34.020 --> 06:36.087
All right, this is good.
Any other suggestions?

06:36.122 --> 06:37.622
Yeah, can you end each show

06:37.657 --> 06:40.125
by trying to pull-start
a very cold chain saw?

06:40.159 --> 06:41.393
Well, that shouldn't
be a problem.

06:41.427 --> 06:42.928
All right, thank you
for being so candid.

06:42.962 --> 06:44.196
Hey, thanks for listening.

06:44.230 --> 06:46.298
I know how hard it is
to take criticism.

06:47.333 --> 06:48.700
Hey, nice boots, Griffin.

06:48.734 --> 06:50.937
They sell men's shoes
where you got those?

06:50.971 --> 06:52.872
<i>PETER: You made a commitment
to these boots, Peter.</i>

06:52.906 --> 06:54.507
<i>These boots are the new you,</i>

06:54.541 --> 06:55.841
<i>and no one will shake that.</i>

06:55.876 --> 06:58.644
Yee-haw, ride 'em, cowgirl!

06:58.679 --> 07:00.446
<i>PETER: Okay, you can take
the boots off at lunch.</i>

07:00.480 --> 07:02.114
<i>Go to the gym.
Have a workout.</i>

07:02.149 --> 07:03.616
<i>Come back in your sneakers.</i>

07:03.650 --> 07:05.685
<i>If anyone asks, you forgot
the boots in your locker.</i>

07:05.719 --> 07:07.119
<i>Just make it to lunch.</i>

07:07.154 --> 07:08.988
Those boots are
made for walkin'.

07:09.022 --> 07:10.523
Up to guys' butts.

07:10.557 --> 07:12.692
(laughing)

07:12.726 --> 07:14.493
Hey, fellas.
Hey.

07:17.898 --> 07:19.031
TOM TUCKER:
Good evening, Quahog.

07:19.066 --> 07:20.933
Tonight, Channel Five
mourns the loss

07:20.968 --> 07:22.235
of a dear colleague.

07:22.269 --> 07:23.703
My moustache.

07:23.737 --> 07:26.005
And as per the wishes
of my moustache,

07:26.039 --> 07:28.541
his ashes were sprinkled
off the coast of Acapulco

07:28.575 --> 07:29.709
where he was born.

07:29.743 --> 07:31.377
Well, that'll do it for us here.

07:31.411 --> 07:32.712
Thanks for watching
Channel Five,

07:32.746 --> 07:34.747
the most trusted name in news.

07:37.150 --> 07:39.352
Ah, crap.

07:39.386 --> 07:41.387
Oh, come on.

07:43.223 --> 07:45.392
Let's go, Tom.

07:45.426 --> 07:46.960
Work, damn it!

07:46.995 --> 07:48.028
What the hell?

07:48.062 --> 07:49.363
What's going on
with the news?

07:49.397 --> 07:51.565
This is terrible!
Yeah, has he lost his mind?

07:51.599 --> 07:53.000
Well, I'll be damned.

07:53.034 --> 07:55.202
If I knew he was gonna do
all that stuff I told him,

07:55.236 --> 07:56.536
I would've told him
more stuff.

07:56.571 --> 07:57.738
What?

07:57.772 --> 07:59.740
Peter, you told him
to do this crap?

07:59.774 --> 08:01.275
Yeah, he came to my house
when he found out

08:01.309 --> 08:03.343
I was a Nielsen family,
asked what I wanted to see.

08:03.378 --> 08:04.911
Hey, hey, you know
what would be cool?

08:04.946 --> 08:07.247
If he did the news with
a family of prairie dogs,

08:07.282 --> 08:08.882
and whenever he said
something sad,

08:08.916 --> 08:10.984
they'd pop their heads up,
all concerned.

08:11.019 --> 08:12.686
Peter, you sure that's
such a good idea?

08:12.720 --> 08:14.921
People rely on the local news
to provide them with

08:14.956 --> 08:17.724
several stories a year on how
saltwater taffy is made.

08:17.759 --> 08:19.660
Yeah, if you're
a Nielsen family,

08:19.694 --> 08:21.595
it seems like you
should maybe be

08:21.629 --> 08:23.096
a little more thoughtful
with your choices.

08:23.131 --> 08:24.264
What are you talking about?

08:24.299 --> 08:25.499
I'm just having a little fun.

08:25.533 --> 08:26.967
For God's sakes,
I've just been handed

08:27.001 --> 08:28.635
the coolest freaking toy
on the planet.

08:28.670 --> 08:32.005
Well, you know, except for
Hungry Hungry Alec Baldwins.

08:33.875 --> 08:36.610
Hey, I'm not... I'm not
even touching the lever.

08:41.417 --> 08:43.918
Chilling news
from Long Island Sound,

08:43.952 --> 08:46.187
as a four-passenger prop plane
on its way to East Hampton

08:46.221 --> 08:48.256
spun into the surf
off Montauk Point.

08:49.091 --> 08:51.459
There were no survivors.

08:51.493 --> 08:53.961
Oh, that's so great, I just
called him on the way home!

08:53.996 --> 08:56.531
Peter, I'm not sure this
is entirely responsible.

08:56.565 --> 08:57.865
I don't see what
the big deal is.

08:57.900 --> 08:59.467
I was just trying
to make the show better.

08:59.501 --> 09:01.369
Hell, I wish I could do it
with all the shows.

09:01.403 --> 09:03.104
Yeah, well, you only have
one Nielsen box.

09:03.138 --> 09:04.872
You don't have the clout
to affect national shows.

09:04.907 --> 09:06.107
Damn it.

09:06.141 --> 09:07.508
I guess that means
I'll never get to see

09:07.543 --> 09:09.544
<i>an episode of Superman
where Clark Kent and Lois Lane</i>

09:09.578 --> 09:11.112
finally get together.

09:11.146 --> 09:12.413
Lois, I love you,

09:12.448 --> 09:15.683
and I want there to be
no more secrets between us.

09:15.718 --> 09:17.352
I am Superman.

09:17.386 --> 09:18.686
Oh, my God.

09:18.721 --> 09:20.555
The only thing that can
kill me is kryptonite.

09:20.589 --> 09:22.090
Or latex.

09:22.124 --> 09:23.257
Or lambskin.

09:23.292 --> 09:24.992
What about polyurethane?
All that.

09:25.027 --> 09:25.993
All that stuff.

09:26.028 --> 09:27.995
(knock at door)

09:28.030 --> 09:29.297
Hi, folks.

09:29.331 --> 09:31.366
Just thought I'd stop by
and make sure your equipment

09:31.400 --> 09:33.502
is working properly and see
if you have any questions.

09:33.536 --> 09:35.170
Yeah, is something wrong
with our remote?

09:35.205 --> 09:36.939
No matter how low
I turn the volume,

09:36.973 --> 09:38.941
Aziz Ansari is always
shouting at me.

09:38.975 --> 09:40.609
What did I do?

09:40.643 --> 09:42.411
Thank you.
I think we're good.

09:42.445 --> 09:43.912
Everything seems
to be going well.

09:43.947 --> 09:44.980
Okay, great.

09:45.014 --> 09:46.515
Well, I'm just gonna
change out the card

09:46.549 --> 09:48.817
on your unit real quick
and I'll be on my way.

10:00.797 --> 10:02.097
Well, we're all set.

10:02.132 --> 10:03.132
Thanks for your time.

10:03.166 --> 10:04.500
No, thank you, pal.

10:04.534 --> 10:05.868
And hey, you've been
working hard.

10:05.902 --> 10:07.536
Why don't you take the
rest of the day off?

10:07.570 --> 10:09.872
Here's two tickets to Sandra
Bernhard's one-woman show.

10:09.906 --> 10:11.073
Wow, thanks!

10:11.107 --> 10:12.241
Yeah, and they're
great seats.

10:12.275 --> 10:13.609
They're right in
the gap of her teeth.

10:13.643 --> 10:15.177
Social media?

10:15.211 --> 10:16.845
More like a social disease.

10:16.880 --> 10:17.846
(audience laughs)

10:17.881 --> 10:19.815
Ha! That's funny!

10:23.853 --> 10:26.155
Peter, what the hell's
going on here?

10:26.189 --> 10:28.591
Lois, we're no longer
one Nielsen family.

10:28.626 --> 10:30.493
We're 100.

10:30.528 --> 10:31.828
More boxes, more power.

10:31.862 --> 10:33.663
And I got some ideas
to make TV better.

10:35.833 --> 10:36.800
(phone rings)

10:36.834 --> 10:38.635
<i>Hello, Mad Men
production office.</i>

10:38.669 --> 10:39.769
Yeah, Peter Griffin here.

10:39.804 --> 10:41.271
Could I speak with
Jon Hamm, please?

10:41.305 --> 10:42.539
One moment.

10:42.573 --> 10:43.540
(phone rings)

10:43.574 --> 10:45.208
Hello?
Hello, Jon Hamm?

10:45.242 --> 10:46.476
Peter Griffin,
Nielsen family.

10:46.510 --> 10:48.011
Listen, did I catch
you at a good time,

10:48.045 --> 10:50.513
or are you and the critics busy
sucking each other's butts?

10:50.548 --> 10:51.648
Excuse me?

10:51.682 --> 10:53.149
Look, your show
is really boring.

10:53.184 --> 10:54.451
But don't worry,
I got some ideas

10:54.485 --> 10:55.585
on how you
can jazz it up.

10:55.619 --> 10:57.420
Listen, I don't need
your suggestions, pal.

10:57.455 --> 11:00.023
I've been a big celebrity
for a year and a half now.

11:00.057 --> 11:01.591
Okay, if that's
how you're gonna be.

11:01.625 --> 11:03.193
We'll see how
this plays out.

11:03.227 --> 11:05.495
<i>Lois, we're not watching
Mad Men no more.</i>

11:08.065 --> 11:09.999
(phone ringing)

11:10.034 --> 11:11.000
Hello?

11:11.035 --> 11:12.602
Look, I may have been
a little rash.

11:12.636 --> 11:14.270
Our ratings
have dropped 50%.

11:14.305 --> 11:16.372
Whatever suggestions
you have, I'll listen.

11:18.476 --> 11:19.843
And so, gentlemen,
in baseball,

11:19.877 --> 11:21.979
three strikes
and you're out.

11:22.013 --> 11:23.781
But three Lucky Strikes...

11:23.815 --> 11:25.916
and you're in.

11:25.951 --> 11:27.117
Nice try, Don.

11:27.152 --> 11:28.552
But I'm afraid
we're going to have

11:28.587 --> 11:29.887
to take our business
elsewhere.

11:29.921 --> 11:32.022
Oh? don't think so.

11:35.427 --> 11:37.895
<i>(playing Star Wars theme)</i>

11:41.299 --> 11:43.067
What the hell was that?

11:43.101 --> 11:44.535
I'll tell you
what it was, Lois.

11:44.569 --> 11:45.703
It was awesome.

11:45.737 --> 11:47.371
<i>And wait'll
you see Breaking Bad.</i>

11:47.405 --> 11:49.874
I don't know what it was,
but now it's on roller skates.

11:52.077 --> 11:54.011
Hi, NBC,
this is Peter Griffin.

11:54.045 --> 11:55.913
Listen, you guys
are doing a great job.

11:55.947 --> 11:59.683
If anybody knows what America
wants in the '90s, it's NBC.

11:59.718 --> 12:01.619
But I just have
one small request:

12:01.653 --> 12:04.622
I like Dateline, but I really
hate waiting two hours

12:04.656 --> 12:06.223
to find out who the killer is.

12:06.258 --> 12:08.759
<i>ANNOUNCER: Tonight on Dateline,
a woman murdered.</i>

12:08.793 --> 12:10.461
<i>Was it her ex-boyfriend?</i>

12:10.495 --> 12:11.962
<i>Yes, it was.</i>

12:11.997 --> 12:13.063
I knew it.

12:13.098 --> 12:15.467
I knew it was the ex-boyfriend.

12:18.871 --> 12:20.472
"Sleep tight, truck.

12:20.506 --> 12:22.908
"Sleep tight, firefly.

12:22.942 --> 12:25.243
"Sleep tight, chair.

12:25.278 --> 12:27.612
Sleep tight, bird."

12:27.647 --> 12:28.747
You see that, Peter?

12:28.781 --> 12:30.015
You see the bird?

12:30.049 --> 12:31.216
Bird.

12:31.250 --> 12:32.951
Okay, we'll, uh,
pick up the rest tomorrow.

12:32.985 --> 12:36.154
Uh, now, I'm just gonna vamp for
a while with some random noises.

12:36.188 --> 12:37.789
Hee-hee!

12:37.823 --> 12:39.958
Heya, heya, heya.

12:39.992 --> 12:41.993
(grumbling, groaning)

12:42.028 --> 12:43.361
Uh-heh, uh-heh...

12:43.396 --> 12:45.630
(gibbering)

12:48.501 --> 12:49.467
Okay, good night, Peter.

12:49.502 --> 12:50.535
Good night, Dave.

12:50.570 --> 12:51.903
LETTERMAN:
And, uh, here's Paul

12:51.938 --> 12:53.505
to play you to sleep
with a lullaby.

12:53.539 --> 12:55.006
PAUL (off-key):
♪ Hey, lullaby... ♪

12:55.041 --> 12:56.374
♪ Oh, lullaby ♪

12:56.409 --> 12:58.243
♪ Hey, you, lullaby... ♪

12:58.277 --> 12:59.277
Stop, no, stop.

12:59.312 --> 13:00.278
Stop.

13:00.313 --> 13:01.980
I forgot, he's terrible.

13:05.017 --> 13:08.053
<i>TV ANNOUNCER: We now return to
Cops With Banana Guns.</i>

13:08.087 --> 13:10.456
Freeze!

13:10.490 --> 13:12.525
Is that...
is that a banana?

13:12.559 --> 13:13.926
Don't worry
about what it is.

13:13.961 --> 13:15.695
I'm still a cop.

13:15.729 --> 13:16.963
Whoa, hold on.

13:16.997 --> 13:18.965
All-All right, just...
just take it easy.

13:18.999 --> 13:21.067
This can go
a couple of ways.

13:21.101 --> 13:23.302
<i>What the hell
did Peter do to Cops?!</i>

13:23.337 --> 13:25.771
Bonnie!
Come push me out in a huff!

13:30.711 --> 13:32.144
Peter, what is this show?

13:32.179 --> 13:34.480
<i>It's called Creeping Up
on the Kardashians.</i>

13:34.514 --> 13:36.215
See that guy with the
ponytail in the background?

13:36.249 --> 13:38.384
He sneaks up and
scares the girls

13:38.418 --> 13:39.852
while they're
starting businesses

13:39.886 --> 13:41.320
or getting
their fat waxed.

13:41.355 --> 13:42.588
(all scream)

13:42.623 --> 13:43.689
What the hell?!

13:45.392 --> 13:46.859
(crowd clamoring)

13:46.893 --> 13:48.995
There they are!
That's the Nielsen family!

13:49.029 --> 13:50.496
You ruined television!

13:50.530 --> 13:52.765
Now it's just
a big, old, silly mess!

13:52.799 --> 13:55.101
Oh, God! An angry mob!

13:55.135 --> 13:58.037
I've got to swallow all my
valuables and get out of here!

14:09.884 --> 14:11.451
Did you see the mob?

14:11.486 --> 14:12.586
Did I see the mob?

14:12.620 --> 14:14.021
Why else am I here?

14:17.598 --> 14:19.566
(clamoring)

14:19.600 --> 14:21.968
Oh, my God, Peter,
they're really angry!

14:22.003 --> 14:23.636
Say something!

14:23.671 --> 14:24.721
W-Wait.
What the hell's going on?

14:24.755 --> 14:26.139
What do you mean,
I ruined television?

14:26.173 --> 14:28.208
<i>You put a real cougar
on Cougar Town,</i>

14:28.242 --> 14:29.676
and now that cougar's dead

14:29.710 --> 14:32.445
because Courtney Cox ripped it
apart with her teeth and claws!

14:32.480 --> 14:36.149
<i>You turned Anderson Cooper 360
into Anderson Cooper 720!</i>

14:36.183 --> 14:37.684
He's turning around too much!

14:37.718 --> 14:40.086
<i>You converted The Biggest Loser
to the metric system!</i>

14:40.121 --> 14:42.088
Now it feels like
they're not losing enough!

14:42.123 --> 14:43.590
Aw, the hell with you guys!

14:43.624 --> 14:46.192
You're just jealous 'cause I get
to say what's on TV now!

14:46.227 --> 14:48.294
I am a Nielsen god!

14:50.297 --> 14:52.298
(cheering)

14:54.702 --> 14:55.902
Sorry, y'all.

14:55.936 --> 14:58.505
That's the first time
I ever throwed anything.

15:03.211 --> 15:05.746
Well, if it isn't
Mr. Nielsen himself.

15:05.781 --> 15:07.948
Nurse, who's the worst
doctor in this hospital?

15:07.983 --> 15:09.183
You are,
Dr. Hartman.

15:09.217 --> 15:10.851
Good.
Put Hartman on this bozo.

15:10.886 --> 15:12.219
Hey, what can
I do for you?

15:12.254 --> 15:14.255
Please, Doc, you got to
help me with this nasty gash.

15:14.289 --> 15:15.289
What seems
to be the problem?

15:15.323 --> 15:16.690
No, it's my husband.

15:16.725 --> 15:18.926
Oh. Well, you've got a lot
of nerve coming in here

15:18.960 --> 15:20.161
after what you
did to television.

15:20.195 --> 15:21.328
Now, get out!

15:21.363 --> 15:23.230
Please, Doctor,
you've got to help him.

15:23.265 --> 15:25.566
You took an oath when
you went to medical school.

15:25.600 --> 15:27.401
I took a lot of things when
I went to medical school.

15:27.436 --> 15:29.203
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I have to answer this.

15:29.237 --> 15:30.404
Hello?

15:30.439 --> 15:32.206
Ah, Hartman!

15:36.945 --> 15:38.079
Hey, guys.
How you doing?

15:38.113 --> 15:39.113
Not so good, Peter.

15:39.147 --> 15:40.247
Yeah, me, either.

15:40.282 --> 15:42.283
Thanks to you,
TV's a vast wasteland.

15:42.317 --> 15:43.551
You know how
I know that phrase?

15:43.585 --> 15:44.919
I read it in a book,
you monster!

15:44.953 --> 15:46.554
Aw, come on, let me
make it up to you.

15:46.588 --> 15:47.588
Let me buy you a beer.

15:47.622 --> 15:49.323
No, that seat's taken.

15:49.357 --> 15:50.391
Move along, Peter.

15:50.425 --> 15:52.093
What are you
talking about?

15:52.127 --> 15:53.128
You guys are my pals.

15:53.162 --> 15:54.229
We used to be, Peter.

15:54.263 --> 15:55.330
Now, scram.

15:55.364 --> 15:57.566
Well, fine,
I'll sit at the bar.

15:57.600 --> 15:59.201
Not at my bar, you won't.

15:59.235 --> 16:00.502
Get out of here!

16:00.536 --> 16:02.637
Geez, I can't
show my face anywhere.

16:02.672 --> 16:05.173
I might as well be back
doing public radio.

16:05.208 --> 16:06.575
This is Peter Griffin,

16:06.609 --> 16:09.945
<i>and you're listening
to Book Talk on WRNI.</i>

16:09.979 --> 16:11.246
Today we'll be discussing

16:11.280 --> 16:13.115
Bret Easton Ellis's
popular work,

16:13.149 --> 16:16.852
<i>Less Than Zero, a tale
of privilege, detachment</i>

16:16.886 --> 16:19.054
and youthful alienation.

16:19.088 --> 16:20.922
(taking a long, loud sip of tea)

16:22.592 --> 16:24.259
But first,
a word from our sponsor,

16:24.293 --> 16:26.495
Westin's Golden Soda Biscuits.

16:26.529 --> 16:28.196
I'm enjoying one right now.

16:28.231 --> 16:30.332
(crunches biscuit)

16:30.366 --> 16:31.800
Mmm.

16:31.834 --> 16:35.770
(sips, then crunches)

16:35.805 --> 16:37.506
Mmm.

16:37.540 --> 16:40.909
(sips tea, crunches biscuit)

16:40.943 --> 16:42.511
Mmm.

16:42.545 --> 16:46.047
(sips tea, crunches biscuit)

16:49.186 --> 16:50.753
(sips tea)

16:50.787 --> 16:52.788
Mmm.

16:56.260 --> 16:58.561
<i>That concludes
today's session of Book Talk.</i>

16:58.595 --> 17:01.330
Tune in tomorrow when we will
look at John Kennedy Toole's

17:01.365 --> 17:04.433
<i>unheralded early work,
The Neon Bible.</i>

17:08.405 --> 17:09.805
Hey, what's wrong, Peter?

17:09.840 --> 17:11.340
I miss my friends, Brian.

17:11.375 --> 17:13.676
I mean, I was having fun
with those Nielsen boxes,

17:13.710 --> 17:15.244
but what's the point

17:15.279 --> 17:17.880
if I don't got Joe and
Quagmire to enjoy it with me?

17:17.915 --> 17:20.716
I guess I shouldn't have
messed with television.

17:20.751 --> 17:22.718
Well, it's not
exactly your fault.

17:22.753 --> 17:24.120
The networks never should
have listened to you

17:24.154 --> 17:25.354
in the first place.

17:25.389 --> 17:27.023
This is exactly what
makes bad television:

17:27.057 --> 17:28.958
pandering to the lowest
common denominator.

17:28.992 --> 17:30.593
So what do I do, Brian?

17:30.627 --> 17:32.128
Well, you still
have these boxes.

17:32.162 --> 17:35.064
That means you still have the
power to influence television.

17:35.098 --> 17:37.166
Maybe you can use that
power to help restore TV

17:37.201 --> 17:38.301
to the way it was.

17:38.335 --> 17:39.502
You're right, Brian.

17:39.536 --> 17:41.504
Maybe if I watch
smart, quality shows,

17:41.538 --> 17:43.173
that'll help get things back
to the way they were.

17:43.208 --> 17:45.609
We can use these boxes
for good and...

17:46.744 --> 17:48.278
What the hell?!

17:48.313 --> 17:52.015
<i>That's for adding another tree
to One Tree Hill!</i>

17:52.050 --> 17:54.484
Oh, my God, he destroyed
every last box!

17:54.519 --> 17:55.786
Holy crap!

17:55.820 --> 17:57.354
We're sunk now, Peter.

17:57.388 --> 18:00.724
There goes your one chance to
get TV back to the way it was.

18:00.758 --> 18:02.626
Wait a minute.
Maybe not, Brian.

18:02.660 --> 18:05.462
I think I just got an idea.

18:05.496 --> 18:07.197
Aah!
I got glass in my face!

18:07.232 --> 18:09.666
Oh, crap.
Now I forgot what it was.

18:09.701 --> 18:10.734
I got it!

18:10.768 --> 18:12.236
Aah! Son of a bitch!

18:15.840 --> 18:16.873
You know who I hate?

18:16.908 --> 18:17.908
The troops.

18:17.942 --> 18:19.243
Yeah, me, too.

18:19.277 --> 18:20.777
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
who are you?

18:20.812 --> 18:21.979
I'm Peter Griffin.

18:22.013 --> 18:23.380
I'm the guy
who ruined television,

18:23.414 --> 18:24.781
and I'm the guy
who's gonna fix it.

18:24.816 --> 18:25.816
Guys!

18:25.850 --> 18:26.850
I broke television,

18:26.884 --> 18:28.385
and now you have
to help me fix it!

18:28.419 --> 18:29.519
Yah-ha!

18:29.554 --> 18:31.855
Looks like this is one
we beat you to.

18:35.727 --> 18:37.795
Gentlemen, I have
gathered you all here today

18:37.830 --> 18:40.298
because you are the creators
of what television used to be

18:40.332 --> 18:41.699
before I ruined it.

18:41.734 --> 18:44.502
And we need to rebuild
television from the ground up.

18:44.536 --> 18:47.438
So, I'm gonna need
all your best ideas.

18:47.473 --> 18:50.174
J.J. Abrams, you take
wonder and complexity

18:50.209 --> 18:52.277
and present it in a way that
no one can possibly understand.

18:52.311 --> 18:53.544
Whaddaya got?!

18:53.579 --> 18:55.513
I've got an alien
that goes back in time

18:55.547 --> 18:58.416
and encounters a koala bear
in an Eastern European town.

18:58.450 --> 18:59.951
Totally confused.
Do it!

18:59.985 --> 19:02.487
Okay, now, we're gonna need
15 workplace comedies

19:02.521 --> 19:04.355
where people talk
to the camera for some reason.

19:04.390 --> 19:06.391
You, you, you and you-- go.

19:07.459 --> 19:08.760
When Peter told me to make

19:08.794 --> 19:10.128
a workplace comedy
where people talk

19:10.162 --> 19:11.429
to the camera, I thought...

19:11.463 --> 19:13.097
Not now!
I mean, go do a show!

19:13.132 --> 19:15.500
Don't-don't do
that thing here.

19:15.534 --> 19:16.534
Huh.

19:16.568 --> 19:17.835
Wonder if I can
pull off one of those

19:17.870 --> 19:19.871
"can you believe what
I have to put up with" looks

19:19.905 --> 19:21.205
to the camera.

19:24.143 --> 19:26.844
<i>Okay, Mark Burnett, you did
Survivor and The Apprentice.</i>

19:26.879 --> 19:29.647
Can you give me a reality show
where people do horrible,

19:29.682 --> 19:31.050
unforgiveable things
to each other

19:31.084 --> 19:32.751
for embarrassingly
small sums of money?

19:32.786 --> 19:33.919
I got some ideas.

19:33.953 --> 19:36.755
Here's a nickel,
pull down your pants.

19:36.790 --> 19:37.990
There's a show.

19:38.024 --> 19:39.291
Yah-ha! Go!

19:40.727 --> 19:42.094
All right, now,
who's gonna make a show

19:42.128 --> 19:43.195
about horrible
New Jersey freaks?

19:43.229 --> 19:44.363
You know what?
I don't care.

19:44.397 --> 19:45.397
Just someone, do it!

19:46.433 --> 19:47.633
Okay, Dick Wolf,

19:47.667 --> 19:49.702
<i>make the same Law and Order
six times.</i>

19:49.736 --> 19:51.704
Oh, and also,
could you marry Matt Weiner

19:51.738 --> 19:53.806
'cause I want your name
to be Dick "Weener."

19:53.840 --> 19:55.974
Okay, but can I go by
"Dick Wolf-Weener"?

19:56.009 --> 19:57.943
Oh, my God, yes!
Yes! Yes!

19:57.977 --> 19:59.578
Okay, Bravo people,
go find women fighting.

19:59.612 --> 20:01.046
No, you know what,
just find women.

20:01.081 --> 20:02.314
They'll end up fighting.

20:02.349 --> 20:04.783
All right, everyone who's left,
make a talent show.

20:04.818 --> 20:06.485
We are done.

20:06.519 --> 20:09.755
Oh, Kelsey Grammer,
what are you still doing here?

20:09.789 --> 20:11.090
I-I have nothing left
for you.

20:11.124 --> 20:12.291
I'm... I'm sorry.

20:12.325 --> 20:16.028
Ah. Then I shall take
my ease on the lanai.

20:16.062 --> 20:17.696
I don't care
what you do now.

20:21.835 --> 20:24.136
<i>TV ANNOUNCER: We now return
to Mike and Molly.</i>

20:24.170 --> 20:26.005
Have you decided
what you'd like to order?

20:26.040 --> 20:27.540
Yes, the chopped salad?

20:27.575 --> 20:29.275
I'll have everything
except that.

20:29.310 --> 20:30.343
(studio audience laughing)

20:30.378 --> 20:31.444
(laughing)

20:31.479 --> 20:32.846
That waiter's like, "What?!"

20:32.880 --> 20:33.980
Well, you did it, Peter.

20:34.014 --> 20:35.715
You got TV back to normal.

20:35.750 --> 20:37.851
Yeah, guys,
I'm sorry for screwing up

20:37.885 --> 20:39.119
all your favorite shows.

20:39.153 --> 20:40.387
Ah, that's okay, Peter.

20:40.421 --> 20:41.388
So, what do you say?

20:41.422 --> 20:42.689
Are we pals again?

20:42.723 --> 20:44.268
Ah, course we are.
You bet.

20:44.269 --> 20:46.069
Well, let's drink
to having TV

20:46.104 --> 20:48.639
back in the hands of people
who know what they're doing.

20:49.865 --> 20:51.766
<i>I think Zack and Cody
would be funnier</i>

20:51.800 --> 20:53.768
if they did the show
in their underpants.

20:53.769 --> 21:54.769
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru